$DIR/test.p:8:2: missing case in switch on c (Color): Blue (add it or a default case)
    A switch on an enum value that has no default case must list every member.
    That way, adding a member to the enum shows every switch that needs to
    handle it.
    Add a case for each missing member, or a default case if the remaining
    members share one action.
    Go does not check this. Plutonium does, because an enum is a closed set of
    values, so the compiler can tell when one is forgotten.
    (see "Switch statements" in the Plutonium spec, section 12.9)
    (run "pluto explain E2312" for a longer explanation)
